# Learning Outcomes and Project Report

## Course/Project: BCIS Subscription Billing and Collection System

### Learning Outcomes Expected
1. Apply software engineering principles (requirements, design, implementation, testing, documentation).
2. Design and implement a 3-tier system (Electron desktop + Fastify API + PostgreSQL).
3. Apply RBAC, authentication, audit trails, and security best practices.
4. Implement financial integrity (money handling, allocations, immutable records, receipts).
5. Work with reporting (PDF/XLSX/CSV), backups/restores, and data integrity.
6. Practice testing (unit, integration, E2E) and evidence-based verification.

### System Functionality Summary
- Authentication & RBAC (OWNER, ADMIN, CASHIER, SUPERVISOR, AUDITOR, TECHNICIAN, VIEWER)
- Master data: plans, subscribers, services, areas, collectors
- Billing: cycles, invoices, corrections, statements, ledger  
- Payments: oldest-due-first allocation, advance credit, GCash verification, void/reversal, receipts
- Collections: routes, remittances, shortage/overage, two-person reconciliation
- Receivables: aging, suspension/reconnection, service history
- Reports & dashboard: KPIs, 9 reports, exports (PDF/XLSX/CSV)
- Backups: pg_dump/pg_restore, integrity, AT-12 verified
- Audit logging with redaction

### Key Metrics
- Phases 1–10: 35/35 checklist items complete (100%)
- Tests: 200 unit, 186 integration, 21 E2E — all passing
- Typecheck/lint clean; production build successful
- Deliverables: ERD, User Manual, Samples, Demo Script, Release Notes, TEST_EVIDENCE, Screenshots (24)

